Expected elements: present

No must-show item is absent and no must-not-show item appears; the light surface is the capture's theme axis, not a register error. Structurally this is disciplined: all three pane headers rule off at y=94, the Values type column and the Call Trace opcode column both right-align at x=1518, every Transaction value right-aligns at x=1906, and the identity bar runs a clean 8/16/24 scale.

The new vertical fade works. In the Code pane line 61 and its line number both dissolve (L36 to L204 over y1046-1072); in the Transaction pane the RAW block's own grey background fades with it, so nothing terminates on a hard edge. It reads as "more below", not as a cut. It is at the weak end: the vertical ramp is ~26px against ~48px for the horizontal fade in the same pane, so exactly one line falls inside it. At 48px a second, near-gone line would appear and remove all doubt.

Last round's measurement holds. Tabbed region: 347px empty below the "By call order" footer, 57.8% of its 600px. Values: 121px, 30.3% of 399px. Column content totals 529px of 1007px, so no row re-split fixes it — the lever is still the column. The widest frame row leaves 131px between its label end (x1353) and the opcode column (x1484) while the Code pane truncates line 40 mid-identifier at x916.

Fixes, in order: narrow the nav column and give the width to Code; move the DATA hairline above its label.

Rating: 7/10

